[6.283283, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1m=== STEP 1: a real project, and a second history opened underneath it\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[6.325567, "o", "  - project: /tmp/checkpoint-demo.QndqNY/mnt/sandbox/acme-api (5 files, an empty dir, an exec bit, a symlink)\r\n  - store:   /tmp/checkpoint-demo.QndqNY/mnt/sandbox/store (the history lives outside the project, which is the whole point)\r\n\u001b[2m$ checkpoint doctor --root /tmp/checkpoint-demo.QndqNY/mnt/sandbox/acme-api --store /tmp/checkpoint-demo.QndqNY/mnt/sandbox/store\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[6.330521, "o", "\u001b]11;?\u001b\\\u001b[6n"]
[6.345218, "o", "ok    kernel                Linux 6.12.76-linuxkit is supported (needs 5.1+; change feed needs 5.17+)\r\nok    fanotify capability   fanotify armed and released successfully (a real group was created and marked)\r\nok    workspace             /tmp/checkpoint-demo.QndqNY/mnt/sandbox/acme-api: 5 files, 240 bytes to protect\r\nok    workspace filesystem  ext2/ext3/ext4: change feed available (deletions are attributed; checkpoints scale with changes, not tree size)\r\nok    store location        /tmp/checkpoint-demo.QndqNY/mnt/sandbox/store: writable, out of the workspace tree\r\nWARN  store free space      only 223.4 MB free of 241.1 MB on the store filesystem (/tmp/checkpoint-demo.QndqNY/mnt/sandbox/store): very little room for checkpoints\r\n                            remedy: free space on that filesystem, or pass --store DIR on a larger one; `checkpoint prune --keep-days N` reclaims old checkpoints\r\n\r\ncheckpoint will work here, with 1 limitation above (WARN).\r\n"]
[6.346906, "o", "\u001b[2m$ checkpoint protect --store /tmp/checkpoint-demo.QndqNY/mnt/sandbox/store /tmp/checkpoint-demo.QndqNY/mnt/sandbox/acme-api\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[6.480459, "o", "\u001b[2m$ checkpoint status --root /tmp/checkpoint-demo.QndqNY/mnt/sandbox/acme-api --store /tmp/checkpoint-demo.QndqNY/mnt/sandbox/store\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[6.490241, "o", "Protection: Protected\r\nRoot: /tmp/checkpoint-demo.QndqNY/mnt/sandbox/acme-api\r\nStore: /tmp/checkpoint-demo.QndqNY/mnt/sandbox/store\r\nStorage: 1.8 kB across 5 objects and 1 checkpoint (oldest just now)\r\nCheckpoints: 1\r\nLast complete checkpoint: 0s ago\r\nComplete baseline: yes\r\nChange feed: active (delete attribution + change-scaled checkpoints)\r\nActive agent sessions: 0\r\nProtecting since: 2026-08-04 20:26:10\r\n"]
[6.505306, "o", "  note: change feed ACTIVE: this filesystem tells checkpoint who deleted a file, so a delete\r\n  note: carries an author like every other change does.\r\n"]
[6.510021, "o", "\u001b[1mSTEP 1 OK\u001b[0m  (227 ms): the session history is open, and its first checkpoint holds the whole project\r\n"]
[6.513381, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1m=== STEP 2: a turn commits itself: refactor two files, delete a third, write outside\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[6.521419, "o", "\u001b[2m$ checkpoint run --root /tmp/checkpoint-demo.QndqNY/mnt/sandbox/acme-api --store /tmp/checkpoint-demo.QndqNY/mnt/sandbox/store -- /tmp/checkpoint-demo.QndqNY/mnt/sandbox/agent_turn.sh\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[6.523866, "o", "checkpoint: local file changes are recoverable; network requests, remote databases, deploys, emails, and other outside effects are NOT.\r\n"]
[6.533977, "o", "AGENT_START 1785875170989\r\n"]
[7.742861, "o", "AGENT_END 1785875172198\r\n"]
[8.109557, "o", "checkpoint 1 DURABLE (7 entries)\r\n"]
[8.113653, "o", "  - two files refactored, scratch.md deleted, one transient created+deleted, one write outside\r\n  - nobody decided when the unit of work was done; the turn boundary did\r\n"]
[8.114415, "o", "\u001b[1mSTEP 2 OK\u001b[0m  (1601 ms): the turn ended and the history committed itself: exactly one durable checkpoint\r\n"]
[8.115066, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1m=== STEP 3: two authors inside one turn: the human edited a different file, mid-turn\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[8.123198, "o", "  - agent turn spanned 1785875170989..1785875172198; the human write landed at 1785875171480, strictly inside it\r\n  - the human process was never a descendant of `checkpoint run`, which is how the history\r\n  - attributes each FILE to an author instead of stamping one author on the whole checkpoint\r\n"]
[8.123845, "o", "\u001b[1mSTEP 3 OK\u001b[0m  (9 ms): one checkpoint, two authors: the file you wrote is recorded as yours, not the agent's\r\n"]
[8.124516, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1m=== STEP 4: reading the log: status + history, and what the history could not hold\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[8.124821, "o", "\u001b[2m$ checkpoint status --root /tmp/checkpoint-demo.QndqNY/mnt/sandbox/acme-api --store /tmp/checkpoint-demo.QndqNY/mnt/sandbox/store\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[8.127311, "o", "Protection: Limited protection\r\nRoot: /tmp/checkpoint-demo.QndqNY/mnt/sandbox/acme-api\r\nStore: /tmp/checkpoint-demo.QndqNY/mnt/sandbox/store\r\nStorage: 4.3 kB across 9 objects and 2 checkpoints (oldest just now)\r\nCheckpoints: 2\r\nLast complete checkpoint: 0s ago\r\nComplete baseline: yes\r\nChange feed: active (delete attribution + change-scaled checkpoints)\r\nActive agent sessions: 0\r\nProtecting since: 2026-08-04 20:26:10\r\nWhy limited:\r\n  ! unprotected changes: the agent wrote 1 time(s) outside the protected folders (not captured, not restorable):\r\n      /tmp/checkpoint-demo.QndqNY/mnt/sandbox/outside/app.conf\r\n      (add folders with: daemon --protect DIR,DIR)\r\n"]
[8.12759, "o", "\u001b[2m$ checkpoint history --root /tmp/checkpoint-demo.QndqNY/mnt/sandbox/acme-api --store /tmp/checkpoint-demo.QndqNY/mnt/sandbox/store\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[8.133622, "o", "#1   2026-08-04 20:26:12  Fully recoverable             run: /tmp/checkpoint-demo.QndqNY/mnt/sandbox/agent_turn.sh\r\n#0   2026-08-04 20:26:10  Fully recoverable             setup\r\n"]
[8.139991, "o", "  - the newest row is the turn that just ran, with a badge for how complete its record is\r\n  - protection is Limited, and status names the exact path the history does not hold\r\n  - a write the history missed is named, never quietly counted as recorded\r\n"]
[8.140704, "o", "\u001b[1mSTEP 4 OK\u001b[0m  (16 ms): the session log is navigable, and honest about the one write it does not hold\r\n"]
[8.147408, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1m=== STEP 5: revert the turn: the agent's changes go, yours stay\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[8.151996, "o", "\u001b[2m$ checkpoint undo --root /tmp/checkpoint-demo.QndqNY/mnt/sandbox/acme-api --store /tmp/checkpoint-demo.QndqNY/mnt/sandbox/store\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[8.162285, "o", "undo of checkpoint 1: reverted 3, removed 1, skipped 0 for review\r\npre-undo checkpoint 2 saved (restore it to undo this undo)\r\n"]
[8.169039, "o", "  - both refactored files reverted, whole-file, because they are the agent's in the record\r\n"]
[8.174459, "o", "  - NOTES.md byte-identical to before the undo: reverting the agent did not revert you\r\n"]
[8.175492, "o", "  - the agent-deleted file came back byte-exact: the delete carried an author too\r\n"]
[8.17626, "o", "  - the revert is itself a checkpoint: the history recorded the state it reverted away from\r\n  note: known gap: edits made by write-temp-then-rename (`sed -i`, and the atomic\r\n  note: saves some editors do) are NOT reverted by undo today. See demo/README.md.\r\n"]
[8.176292, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1m--- 5b: a file you BOTH wrote is refused, never merged (there is no merge here)\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[9.761206, "o", "\u001b[2m$ checkpoint undo --root /tmp/checkpoint-demo.QndqNY/mnt/sandbox/acme-api --store /tmp/checkpoint-demo.QndqNY/mnt/sandbox/store\u001b[0m\r\n  needs review (you also changed it): NOTES.md\r\ncheckpoint: 1 file(s) need review; NOTHING was changed. Rerun with --save-both to revert the rest and keep each conflict's checkpoint version alongside\r\n"]
[9.764167, "o", "  - undo exited 1 and changed nothing at all, not even the files it could have reverted\r\n"]
[9.76508, "o", "\u001b[2m$ checkpoint undo --save-both --root /tmp/checkpoint-demo.QndqNY/mnt/sandbox/acme-api --store /tmp/checkpoint-demo.QndqNY/mnt/sandbox/store\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[9.767335, "o", "undo of checkpoint 3: reverted 0, removed 1, skipped 1 for review\r\n  needs review (you also changed it, left untouched): NOTES.md\r\n"]
[9.767546, "o", "  saved checkpoint version alongside: /tmp/checkpoint-demo.QndqNY/mnt/sandbox/acme-api/NOTES.md.checkpoint-1\r\npre-undo checkpoint 4 saved (restore it to undo this undo)\r\n"]
[9.781068, "o", "  - your file untouched; the version from the history written alongside as NOTES.md.checkpoint-1\r\n  - nothing was line-merged, and nothing of yours was overwritten\r\n"]
[9.784321, "o", "\u001b[1mSTEP 5 OK\u001b[0m  (1637 ms): the turn was reverted per file: the agent's undone, yours kept, shared files refused\r\n"]
[9.78505, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1m=== STEP 6: rm -rf the whole project, then check it back out of the history, byte-exact\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[9.785331, "o", "\u001b[2m$ checkpoint save --root /tmp/checkpoint-demo.QndqNY/mnt/sandbox/acme-api --store /tmp/checkpoint-demo.QndqNY/mnt/sandbox/store --name before-disaster\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[10.138865, "o", "checkpoint 5 \"before-disaster\" DURABLE (10 entries)\r\n"]
[10.175008, "o", "  - recorded 10 paths with modes, symlink targets and content hashes\r\n\u001b[2m$ rm -rf /tmp/checkpoint-demo.QndqNY/mnt/sandbox/acme-api\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[10.176217, "o", "  - the project directory no longer exists\r\n"]
[10.177352, "o", "\u001b[2m$ checkpoint restore --store /tmp/checkpoint-demo.QndqNY/mnt/sandbox/store 5 /tmp/checkpoint-demo.QndqNY/mnt/sandbox/acme-api\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[10.179639, "o", "\u001b]11;?\u001b\\\u001b[6n"]
[10.1867, "o", "restored checkpoint 5 (10 entries) to /tmp/checkpoint-demo.QndqNY/mnt/sandbox/acme-api [coverage: DURABLE]\r\n"]
[10.215835, "o", "  - every path, mode, exec bit, symlink target and byte identical (12 ms)\r\n  - the history was never inside the project, so deleting the project did not touch it\r\n"]
[10.216988, "o", "\u001b[1mSTEP 6 OK\u001b[0m  (432 ms): the working tree was destroyed and rebuilt byte-exact from a history that outlived it\r\n"]
[10.217945, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1m=== STEP 7: a state no commit ever held: a file created and deleted inside one turn\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[10.218372, "o", "\u001b[2m$ checkpoint recover --store /tmp/checkpoint-demo.QndqNY/mnt/sandbox/store /tmp/checkpoint-demo.QndqNY/mnt/sandbox/acme-api\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[10.222957, "o", "/tmp/checkpoint-demo.QndqNY/mnt/sandbox/acme-api/.agent-tmp.json\r\n"]
[10.225228, "o", "\u001b[2m$ checkpoint recover --store /tmp/checkpoint-demo.QndqNY/mnt/sandbox/store --to /tmp/checkpoint-demo.QndqNY/mnt/sandbox/salvage /tmp/checkpoint-demo.QndqNY/mnt/sandbox/acme-api\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[10.235692, "o", "\u001b]11;?\u001b\\\u001b[6n"]
[10.237264, "o", "recovered /tmp/checkpoint-demo.QndqNY/mnt/sandbox/acme-api/.agent-tmp.json -> /tmp/checkpoint-demo.QndqNY/mnt/sandbox/salvage/.agent-tmp.json\r\n"]
[10.238787, "o", "  - no checkpoint ever contained this file: recording is continuous, and checkpoints are only labels over it\r\n  - this is the state git cannot have, because nothing committed while the file existed\r\n"]
[10.239494, "o", "\u001b[1mSTEP 7 OK\u001b[0m  (22 ms): a file that lived only between checkpoints came back byte-exact\r\n"]
[10.240559, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1m=== STEP 8: closing the session\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[10.240665, "o", "\u001b[2m$ checkpoint protect --store /tmp/checkpoint-demo.QndqNY/mnt/sandbox/store --stop /tmp/checkpoint-demo.QndqNY/mnt/sandbox/acme-api\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[10.24249, "o", "\u001b]11;?\u001b\\\u001b[6n"]
[10.373427, "o", "protection stopped for /tmp/checkpoint-demo.QndqNY/mnt/sandbox/acme-api\r\n"]
[10.374249, "o", "\u001b[2m$ checkpoint status --root /tmp/checkpoint-demo.QndqNY/mnt/sandbox/acme-api --store /tmp/checkpoint-demo.QndqNY/mnt/sandbox/store\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[10.378525, "o", "Protection: Not protected (no daemon running for this project)\r\nRoot: /tmp/checkpoint-demo.QndqNY/mnt/sandbox/acme-api\r\nStore: /tmp/checkpoint-demo.QndqNY/mnt/sandbox/store\r\nCheckpoints on record: 7\r\nStorage: 15 kB across 12 objects and 7 checkpoints (1 named, oldest just now)\r\nLast complete checkpoint: 0s ago\r\n"]
[10.38032, "o", "  - daemon stopped and socket removed; the history is still on disk and still checkoutable\r\n"]
[10.383549, "o", "  - size of the whole session history for this demo: 47K\r\n  - sandbox (project, store, daemon) about to be deleted; your machine is unchanged\r\n"]
[10.384818, "o", "\u001b[1mSTEP 8 OK\u001b[0m  (144 ms): recording stopped cleanly, and the session history it wrote is still readable\r\n"]
[10.385904, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1m────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[1mPROVEN ON THIS MACHINE IN 7.0s\u001b[0m. Every line below was asserted against disk state:\r\n  A session ran: an agent refactored 2 files, deleted 1, created and deleted a transient,\r\n"]
[10.385951, "o", "  and wrote outside the project, while a human edited a file alongside it. The turn\r\n  committed itself, with an author per file. The log named the one write it does not\r\n  hold. Reverting the turn undid every agent change and nothing of the human's, and\r\n  refused the file they both wrote rather than merging it (keeping both versions on\r\n  request). After rm -rf, the project was checked back out byte-exact from a history\r\n  that lives outside it. And a file no commit could ever have held, created and deleted\r\n  inside one turn, came back byte-exact.\r\n  Change feed ACTIVE: deletes carried an author, so the agent's delete was reverted\r\n  automatically.\r\n\u001b[1m────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[10.407752, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[10.407815, "o", "# "]
[16.491099, "o", "exit\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
